# EduInsight — Project Rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) first, then [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md).

## Authority

- Product scope: `docs/02-PRD/PRD.md`
- Architecture: `docs/10-References/SystemArchitecture.md` + `docs/decisions/`
- Active work: `docs/07-Sprint-Planning/Sprint3.md`

## Code style

- Python: type hints required; `snake_case` functions, `PascalCase` classes ([CodeStyleGuide](../../docs/10-References/CodeStyleGuide.md))
- Agent tools: docstrings required — LLM uses them to call tools correctly
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*

## Testing

- Backend: `pytest` + `ruff check` in `backend/`
- Frontend: `npm run lint` + `npm test` in `frontend/`
- Full verify: `.\scripts\verify.ps1` from repo root
- Agent evaluation (slow, costs tokens): `.\scripts\verify.ps1 -AgentEval`

## Boundaries

- LLM does not generate ML probabilities — only explains predictions from schema `ml`
- DWH analytics use schema `dwh`, not raw OLTP CRUD tables
- Do not modify `.ai-log/` or course logging hooks

## On agent failure

Ask: what capability was missing, and how can it be made legible and enforceable?
Record friction in `docs/harness/friction-log.md`; fix via rules, decisions, or verify commands.
